{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/194570-newcomers-in-an-ongoing-chronicle","id":194570,"title":"Newcomers in an ongoing chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-11T05:21:33-07:00","id":194570,"title":"Newcomers in an ongoing chronicle","content":"Let's say you are in the middle of a chronicle, and there is a chance of introducing a new player character.<br /> <br /> How Storyteller and players answer to this redevelopment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:31:50-07:00","id":194985,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't be a problem. Either they're a newcomer to the domain/sept/chantry/necropolis/whatever or have just been in the background until now, and now have an interest in the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:42:44-07:00","id":195722,"title":"","content":"Integrating new PCs into an ongoing game can be a tricky business. I've seen it handled well, but also pretty poorly.<br /> <br /> Ideally, you introduce the new PC at a dramatic moment that gets them in good with the group. When the other PCs have been captured, the newcomer shows up to rescue them. When they're fighting a longstanding antagonist, the newcomer crashes through a window guns blazing. Like all good beginnings, you want the new PC's to instantly grab everyone's attention (as opposed to just bumping into them in on the street.)<br /> <br /> It can also be helpful to make the resolution of existing plotlines contingent upon the new PC's involvement. For instance, if the PCs are tracking down an occult artifact, it could wind up in the new PC's possession. It still need the above mentioned punch factor to really work, though. Continuing with the previous example, the GM might trick the PCs into thinking an antagonist beat them to the artifact. Just as they're thinking how screwed they are, the new PC shows up with it safely in hand.<br /> <br /> Giving the newcomer an established connection to existing PCs is also a plus (being a cousin, childhood friend, apprentice at the same chantry, whatever). TV shows do that all the time. However, like in TV shows, a presumed emotional connection can feel hollow until something actually happens to illustrate why these people car about each other.<br /> <br /> Probably the worst time to introduce a new PC is during downtime or some other lull in the action. The other PCs are usually busy with their own concerns and it turns the newcomer into a tagalong. Granted, it's not always possible to introduce new PCs during dramatic moments (particularly if there's a new player, who can drop in whenever). One interim solution is to give the player control of an NPC, or to simply have them join the game a few sessions later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T22:01:28-07:00","id":196030,"title":"","content":"I joined a Play-by-Post Giovanni saga already in progress just before the start of Book 3. I pitched the character and worked on him with the storyteller, and he gave me a prelude forum thread where I could begin to play the character and get him involved in the story. I worked in angles into his background so he would have an instant reason for participating in what the Camarilla characters were doing; hunting down members of the Dunsirn branch of the Giovanni in 1848 London. He was introduced to the other characters at the Court of the Prince of Paris, and the visiting Toreador Justicar almost immediately set them on a hunt for Sabbat agents within the city. <br /> <br /> My advice is to find out from the Storyteller what the next major events he has planned for the chronicle are, and give your character excellent motivation to get directly involved with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}